{"availability":"available","full":"YearsAlso/zoo-framework","name":"zoo-framework","description":"In-process task orchestration for Python: scheduled, observable, stateful — no broker, no cron daemon.","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2023-06-07T12:53:36Z","updated":"2026-10-13T06:30:21Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yearsalso.github.io/zoo-framework/","topics":["agent","ai-agents","asyncio","background-jobs","concurrency","event-driven","framework","job-scheduler","llm","multithreading","no-dependencies","pypi","python","python3","scheduler","state-machine","task-orchestration","task-scheduler","threading","workflow-engine"],"demo":"https://yearsalso.github.io/zoo-framework/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.390Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.390Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.390Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:49.612Z","stars":1,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-13T06:39:42.390Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Python declarative multi-task orchestration framework powering next-gen Agents and workflows","Zoo Framework runs long-lived background tasks in-process — no broker (no Redis / RabbitMQ), no distributed setup, designed so that AI-agent-generated code can drive it: a narrow extension surface, loud failures, and a spec baseline an agent can verify by running tests.","It is for developers who need scheduled, observable, persistent background work embedded in their own process — the in-process alternative to Celery, not a replacement for it."],"features":["Events are isolated per channel; an event can select its response mechanism (first responder only / by priority / all / a named responder). Reactor registration is idempotent — registering the same object twice does not…","State is persisted periodically by StateMachineWorker and once more on shutdown: written to